</surname><given-names>RK</given-names></name><name><surname>Elich</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Fankhauser</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>From seed germination to flowering, light controls plant development via the pigment phytochrome.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>93</volume><fpage>12066</fpage><lpage>12071</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8901532</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000449-Mussig1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mussig</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Lisso</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Coll-Garcia</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Altmann</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Molecular analysis of brassinosteroid action.</article-title><source>Plant Biol</source><volume>8</volume><fpage>291</fpage><lpage>296</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16807820</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000449-Lindsey1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lindsey</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Casson</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Chilley</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Peptides: new signalling molecules in plants.</article-title><source>Trends Plant Sci</source><volume>7</volume><fpage>78</fpage><lpage>83</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11832279</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000449-Gehring1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gehring</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Irving</surname><given-names>HR</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Natriuretic peptides-a class of heterologous molecules in plants.</article-title><source>Int J Biochem Cell Biol</source><volume>35</volume><fpage>1318</fpage><lpage>1322</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12798346</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000449-Gehring2"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gehring</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Irving</surname><given-names>HR</given-names></name><name><surname>Parish</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name></person-group><year>1990</year><article-title>Effects of auxin and abscisic acid on cytosolic calcium and pH in plant cells.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>87</volume><fpage>9645</fpage><lpage>9649</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11607135</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000449-Leyser1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leyser</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>The fall and rise of apical dominance.</article-title><source>Curr Opin Genet Dev</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>468</fpage><lpage>471</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15964756</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000449-Clouse1"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clouse</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Arabidopsis mutants reveal multiple roles for sterols in plant development.</article-title><source>Plant Cell</source><volume>14</volume><fpage>1995</fpage><lpage>2000</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12215500</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000449-Haubrick1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haubrick</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name><name><surname>Assmann</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Brassinosteroids and plant function: some clues, more puzzles.</article-title><source>Plant Cell Environ</source><volume>29</volume><fpage>446</fpage><lpage>457</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17080598</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000449-Li1"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Chory</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>A putative leucine-rich repeat receptor kinase involved in brassinosteroid signal transduction.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>90</volume><fpage>929</fpage><lpage>938</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9298904</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000449-Friedrichsen1"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Friedrichsen</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Joazeiro</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunter</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>J</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Brassinosteroid-insensitive-1 is a ubiquitously expressed leucine-rich repeat receptor serine/ threonine kinase.</article-title><source>Plant Physiol</source><volume>123</volume><fpage>1247</fpage><lpage>1255</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10938344</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000449-Wang1"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>ZY</given-names></name><name><surname>Seto</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Fujioka</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><su